<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giovanni Battista Bogino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1701–1784</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Count Bogino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giovanni Battista Lorenzo Bogino was a Piedmontese statesman and minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-iii-of-sardinia">Charles Emmanuel III of Sardinia</a>, responsible for war and for the affairs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1759 to 1773. He pursued reforms on the island, refounding the universities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cagliari">Cagliari</a> and Sassari in the 1760s, promoting agriculture and encouraging the use of Italian. He fell from power on the accession of Victor Amadeus III.</p></div>
